sitive on $(a,b).$\n\n- If ${f}^{′}(x)<0$ for all $x\\in (a,b),$ then the slope of $f(x)$ is negative on $(a,b).$\n\nFrom the above graph, we can see that ${f}^{′}(x)$ is negative on the intervals $(-\\infty ,-4),$ $(-2,0)$ and $(2,7):$\n\n![](images/60/601ab59d48ed791a0b468ad969a58e5a39d373e670698b3175b62eaf936204f8.png)\n\nTherefore, $f(x)$ is decreasing when  $x\\in (-\\infty ,-4)\\cup (-2,0)\\cup (2,7).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186507494 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078406 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7768eb85-b81d-5f86-b609-5fcaeebe3028" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Increasing and Decreasing Intervals Given the Graph of a Derivative"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c1be330f-e913-5e42-8944-b4cde689560c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507106}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c1be330f-e913-5e42-8944-b4cde689560c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507106} :answer-field/id #uuid "1c7469d3-8121-5a7e-8553-255d494921c1" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507258} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5c456f42-03e1-5f4f-b6ed-a7bcc777e422" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506898}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5c456f42-03e1-5f4f-b6ed-a7bcc777e422" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506898} :answer-field/id #uuid "49a72e5b-d4c2-5c25-a28b-f536baafd3d8" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507280} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "daf370f2-1211-5aca-b3fd-27a33eb6d5d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507152}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "daf370f2-1211-5aca-b3fd-27a33eb6d5d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507152} :answer-field/id #uuid "9e640979-d52e-5b43-ace7-97a3c1d63bf5" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507343}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c277d688-8c79-52bb-ae19-d0f8cd7dbd5e" :question/math-academy-id "q-344945" :question/problem "![](images/f9/f9ecaff65364279019c1cd503fd1c211941cb0022e44bc6f7fdda93a98bd7f34.png)\n\nThe graph of the first derivative $y={f}^{′}(x)$ of the function $f(x)$ intersects the $x$-axis at the points $x=-5,$ $x=-1,$ $x=2,$ and $x=7,$ as shown above. Find all the values of $x$ where the slope of the function $y=f(x)$ is positive.\n\n$x\\in ($\n{{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}$)⋃(2,$\n{{field-3}}$)$" :question/worked-solution "First, we recall the following:\n\n- If ${f}^{′}(x)=0$ for all $x\\in (a,b),$ then the slope of $f(x)$ is equal to zero on $(a,b).$\n\n- If ${f}^{′}(x)>0$ for all $x\\in (a,b),$ then the slope of $f(x)$ is positive on $(a,b).$\n\n- If ${f}^{′}(x)<0$ for all $x\\in (a,b),$ then the slope of $f(x)$ is negative on $(a,b).$\n\nFrom the above graph, we can see that ${f}^{′}(x)$ is positive on the intervals $(-5,-1)$ and $(2,7):$ \n\n![](images/10/1099479c33903078a3e8223fd5635f40cfc85daf045e46e07886a06c3a1bdbe7.png)\n\nTherefore, the slope of the function $f(x)$ is positive when\n\n$$\nx\\in (\\,-5,-1\\,)⋃(2,7\\,).\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186507401 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078406 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7768eb85-b81d-5f86-b609-5fcaeebe3028" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Increasing and Decreasing Intervals Given the Graph of a Derivative"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0d63fa6a-dfb8-540a-beb5-b67a05ed94a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506702}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0d63fa6a-dfb8-540a-beb5-b67a05ed94a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506702} :answer-field/id #uuid "3515176e-8bb6-5675-93b4-e9bfa9b4d3e8" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507267} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "640a4ea2-8cdf-5e3f-94b4-9107e05a9d9d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\infty" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506917}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "640a4ea2-8cdf-5e3f-94b4-9107e05a9d9d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\infty" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506917} :answer-field/id #uuid "5237c6c9-a638-5d50-b2ba-020d7633ab4c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507289} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "24efd74e-b9a4-5d27-87c8-00356a57e76e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506758}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "24efd74e-b9a4-5d27-87c8-00356a57e76e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506758} :answer-field/id #uuid "76674ae6-5330-53b5-a588-92810c21f6f2" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507309}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0751d5ce-14fa-50af-9e34-1f489f4e62f6" :question/math-academy-id "q-344946" :question/problem "![](images/af/afff8f92fcd098ab657807503e9ac339a5e662f23feeffa1617eed44a4e3d93b.png)\n\nThe graph of the first derivative $y={f}^{′}(x)$ of the function $f(x)$ intersects the $x$-axis at the points $x=-6,$ $x=-1,$ and $x=3,$ as shown above. Find all the values of $x$ where the slope of the function $y=f(x)$ is negative.\n\n$x\\in ($\n{{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}$)⋃(-1,$\n{{field-3}}$)$" :question/worked-solution "First, we recall the following:\n\n- If ${f}^{′}(x)=0$ for all $x\\in (a,b),$ then the slope of $f(x)$ is equal to zero on $(a,b).$\n\n- If ${f}^{′}(x)>0$ for all $x\\in (a,b),$ then the slope of $f(x)$ is positive on $(a,b).$\n\n- If ${f}^{′}(x)<0$ for all $x\\in (a,b),$ then the slope of $f(x)$ is negative on $(a,b).$\n\nFrom the above graph, we can see that ${f}^{′}(x)$ is negative on the intervals $(-\\infty ,-6)$ and $(-1,3):$ \n\n![](images/0d/0d326b09364a5a8a02de62e0403fdd64978a61cd85268e8d4c6921e3f3bd6fab.png)\n\nTherefore, the slope of the function $f(x)$ is negative when\n\n$$\nx\\in (\\,-\\infty ,-6\\,)⋃(-1,3\\,).\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186507445 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078406 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7768eb85-b81d-5f86-b609-5fcaeebe3028" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Increasing and Decreasing Intervals Given the Graph of a Derivative"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0bfacb6a-e256-5c8e-934f-448424d2d5e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506698}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0bfacb6a-e256-5c8e-934f-448424d2d5e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506698} :answer-field/id #uuid "42564b93-3ee6-567a-8f8e-de7d1819de34" :